	(text "Must route it using a Kelvin Connection:\n\nDedicated Traces: Draw a thin, dedicated trace directly \nfrom the SP1 pin to the physical copper pad on the \ninside edge of the upper side of the shunt resistor.\n\nDo the same for Ground: Draw another thin, dedicated trace \ndirectly from the SN1 pin to the physical copper pad on the \ninside edge of the bottom side of the shunt resistor. \nDo NOT connect SN1 to your main ground plane anywhere else \nit must only touch ground right at the resistor pad.\n\nRoute them together: \nRoute the SP1 and SN1 traces right next to each other, parallel, \nall the way from the DRV8301 to the resistor. \nThis is called a Differential Pair. \nBecause they are right next to each other, \nany magnetic noise from the motor will hit both wires equally, \nand the DRV8301's amplifier will magically cancel the noise out!"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 135.636 147.32 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(thickness 0.254)
				(bold yes)
				(italic yes)
				(color 255 0 0 1)
			)
		)
